# Bonuscard Odoo — Core Rules

Canonical instructions: `.github/copilot-instructions.md` (read for full detail).

## Product

Odoo 19 addon integrating POS with Bonuscard (loyalty/discount). Primary surface:
Point of Sale. Purchase lifecycle: ValidatePurchase → FinalizePurchase / CancelPurchase.

## Architecture

- Connection config per company; Basic auth via `bonuscard.connector.instance._build_headers`.
- HTTP/payload mapping in `BonuscardApiService`; keep transport separate from Odoo business logic.
- Bonuscard status on contacts is mirrored to **commercial partner** when both share the same normalized phone.
- Partner lookup: phone (digits-only), email, name — dedupe by Bonuscard `id` or `recruitmentCode`.
- Keep all Bonuscard logic in this addon. Configure a POS discount product for unmatched discounts.

## Secrets & Testing

- Never write real credentials into repo files, tests, commits, or PR text.
- Mock HTTP in automated tests. No live or test API calls in CI/default test runs.
- Use `LOCAL_SETUP.md` for Odoo commands. If missing from context, ask the user — do not guess.

## Workflow

Before code edits, confirm: branch goal, done criteria, expected files, non-goals.
If domain behavior is unclear, stay in analysis mode first.
After edits: run/suggest commands from `LOCAL_SETUP.md`; report verified vs not verified.

When fixing tests: get failing test name, error output, repro command, expected behavior.
Fix root cause in production code first; batch-fix matching patterns across files.

## Code Quality

```bash
uv sync --group dev --no-install-project
pre-commit run --all-files
```

Behavior changes require doc updates — see `documentation.mdc` or copilot instructions.
